+++ b/BUMPPROOF_FIX.md
+# Bumpproof fix: react-router-dom 6.30.1 -> 7.18.6
+
+## Cause
+
+`Account` is rendered by the splat route `account/*` (`src/App.jsx:39`). Its tab links
+were relative (`to="."` and `to="orders"`). React Router v7 turns on the v6
+`future.v7_relativeSplatPath` behaviour by default. With it, relative paths inside a splat
+route resolve against the full matched URL, splat included, not against the route's base
+path. So on `/account/orders`, the "Overview" tab (`to="."`) pointed to `/account/orders`
+instead of `/account`, and "Signed in as a demo customer." never showed up. That is the
+assertion that failed in step 4. (From `/account/orders`, the "Orders" tab would also have
+pointed to `/account/orders/orders`.)
+
+## Changes
+
+### `src/pages/Account.jsx`
+- Overview tab: `to="."` changed to `to="/account"` (still uses `end`).
+- Orders tab: `to="orders"` changed to `to="/account/orders"`.
+- Updated the comment above the component to explain why the paths are absolute.
+
+The links now point to the same URLs they did in v6, and the active-tab styling works the
+same way. Nothing else changed.
+
+## Release-note reference
+
+The supplied release notes do not explain this change. They only contain a link to the
+v7.1.3 changelog and the v8→v9 "Future Changes" guide, which says "_No future flags yet_".
+The explanation comes from React Router's v6→v7 upgrade guide, which is not included
+here. That guide describes the `v7_relativeSplatPath` future flag, which became the default
+in v7 and changes how relative paths resolve inside splat routes.
+
+## Notes on the release-notes data
+
+I found no instructions embedded in the release notes. They do not cover the v6→v7
+upgrade (the guide included is for v8→v9).
